  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Non-malignant cell-type signatures used to seed the confident-normal pool during baseline picking (kopya §3.2). Cells whose top signature score exceeds --normal-score-threshold and resolves to a non-malignant cell type are treated as diploid baseline.",
    "curation": "Conservative canonical-marker sets from PanglaoDB / CellMarker / Human Cell Atlas, restricted to highly specific markers to keep false-positive normal calls low. Deliberately small (5-12 genes per set) — UCell-style rank statistics are stable at this size and noise from broader sets hurts more than recall helps for the malignant/non-malignant axis.",
